0-27T08:58:47.943104+00:00","reason_code":"duplicate_diagnostic_target"},{"id":"year_1_1a_or_modelling_reduced_cost_54483e1f_017","difficulty":"challenge","question_type":"conceptual","question":"In the course convention a maximization tableau has objective row $z+\\sum_jq_jx_j=z_0$. Why is the reduced cost of a nonbasic variable $x_j$ equal to $-q_j$ rather than $q_j$?","options":["With other nonbasics at 0, $z=z_0-q_jx_j$.","Reduced costs are defined for minimization.","The simplex method negates the objective.","The basic adjustment flips the sign of $q_j$."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"7978fe6b154253c92845e6bf","time_limit":40,"curation_status":"retired","retired_at":"2026-10-27T08:58:47.943104+00:00","reason_code":"duplicate_diagnostic_target"},{"id":"year_1_1a_or_modelling_reduced_cost_54483e1f_018","difficulty":"challenge","question_type":"conceptual","question":"At the optimum of a maximization LP, product $x_9$ is not made even though its profit per unit, 10, is the highest of all products; its reduced cost is $-2$. Which explanation is consistent with these numbers?","options":["Its profit coefficient was entered as $-2$ by mistake.","Its resource use is worth 12 at the current optimum.","A product with top profit always has reduced cost 0.","Its resource use is worth 8 at the current optimum."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"f842b66be72abcd4ec939911","time_limit":40,"curation_status":"retired","retired_at":"2026-10-27T08:58:47.943104+00:00","reason_code":"duplicate_diagnostic_target"}]}}